      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "HELLO VENETA (2) brings the strongest recent form, having run third in a BM58+ at this track after being sent out favourite, and that followed a decisive CL1 win at Northam where she beat Playing Free by just over two lengths. Her record around 1300m is a major positive and the class drop gives her the right platform. GOLD LILLY (4) is the main danger on consistency and venue suitability, with a close third last start and a prior fourth when she had difficulty getting clear. COULDABEENAHANDBAG (3) has been narrowly beaten at her past two and rarely runs poorly, although her profile is stronger for the placings than as a reliable winner. SHIMARI (5) has earned another look after winning a Mdn at Leonora as an odds-on favourite, but this is a harder meeting and she has to prove that form transfers back to this level. SPANK APPEAL (1) is next best.",
